Tool call input: {'knowledge_bases': ['pubmed_papers'], 'search_rounds_budget': 1, 'search_target': 'Find authoritative ISCD/technical densitometry guidance on lumbar spine DXA analysis regions, vertebral ROI/edge placement, scan analysis quality control, and whether incorrect or inconsistent region boundaries affect reported areal BMD. Need citation or explicit guidance; focus on official positions and technical papers.'}

The search did not identify a direct study or guideline addressing “filling in the bottom of the spine bone map,” and the queried literature was partly noisy. The supported general point is methodological: DXA areal BMD is mineral content divided by projected area, so changing analyzed boundaries/pixels can alter the reported value; the direction and size are not inferable without the specific map/software/image. I’ll record this cautiously, rather than claim a demonstrated clinical effect.

